{
    "type": "game",
    "name": "Nekokami: Internship - The Prologue Adventure",
    "steam_appid": 2825730,
    "required_age": 0,
    "is_free": true,
    "controller_support": "full",
    "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\u2728<u>Nekokami: Internship is a FREE prologue to the full game Nekokami. This prologue contains 20+ Expeditions and roughly 4 hours of story-rich gameplay.</u> </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2825730/extras/5778ad38a16bd1e0bacdeaef246a7579.poster.avif?t=1754614786\" width=616 height=200 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2825730/extras/5778ad38a16bd1e0bacdeaef246a7579.webm?t=1754614786\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2825730/extras/5778ad38a16bd1e0bacdeaef246a7579.mp4?t=1754614786\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>UPDATE: Nekokami - The Human Restoration Project is now in Early Access! \ud83c\udf89 Check out our developer page or scroll down to &quot;More from Rocket-in-Bottle&quot;! \ud83d\ude80</i></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2825730/extras/f78d1cfa558dfd91547a35dadc5a2c0f.avif?t=1754614786\" width=616 height=170 /></span>In this sneak peek of the full game, you will:  </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\ud83c\udf0f Create beautiful worlds of natural habitats and human settlements with strategic, or spontaneous, placement of tiles in a unique hand-drawn-like art style. </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\ud83c\udf0c Follow the beginning of a whimsical yet heart-warming story of Human-Cat friendship, set millennia later in the future. </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\ud83d\udcbc Earn your place in Nekokami Co., your employer, by creating worlds that beat expectations. Or just relax. Your bosses are Cats after all. </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\ud83d\udd2e Befriend a selection of Kami, spirits of the nature and the universe, and see them bring miracles to your work. They are Cats too. What could go wrong?</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2825730/extras/4ef0c006337f014e9463e526c49c92bc.avif?t=1754614786\" width=616 height=200 /></span>\ud83c\udf1f Nekokami Co. is commissioned to manage planets all over the universe. That's a LOT of planets! Environment, biomes and rules differ from Star System to Star System. You will get to visit at least SIX Star Systems during your internship.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\ud83d\udc08 I did mention the Kami*, right? Technically the spirits are the real fellows creating the worlds. As a Planetary Architect, you are basically borrowing their Creative Energy for your own use. You will need to seek their acceptance and approval. Through their friendship, you will potentially learn the secrets of nature and the arcane laws of universe. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2825730/extras/0d7be0eb0198e4dd9614f4a79706b0c3.poster.avif?t=1754614786\" width=616 height=200 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2825730/extras/0d7be0eb0198e4dd9614f4a79706b0c3.webm?t=1754614786\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2825730/extras/0d7be0eb0198e4dd9614f4a79706b0c3.mp4?t=1754614786\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span>*Kami is actually a Japanese word that roughly translates to &quot;spirits and gods&quot;.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>About the Developer</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > This game was made by a tiny tiny independent game studio in Fukuoka. We hope you enjoy it!</p>",
