ranslates to &quot;spirits and gods&quot;.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>About the Developer</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > This game was made by a tiny tiny independent game studio in Fukuoka. We hope you enjoy it!</p>",
    "short_description": "Architect beautiful, peaceful worlds in a far-future where Cats rule the universe. Befriend sometimes-naughty spirits of nature. Manage Humans. Join us in this unique planet-building adventure and get a taste of the full journey!",
    "supported_languages": "English, Japanese, Simplified Chinese",
    "reviews": "\u201cNekokami looks like it'll be intriguing for fans of tile-placing games like Dorfromantik, though with a more objective focused set of challenges and puzzles rather than open-ended score chasing.\u201d<br>PC Gamer<br><br>\u201c(Translated) I felt that even the early tutorial-like stages had a sufficient amount of content, but there are still plenty of stages to play and enjoy!\u201d<br>Indie Freaks<br>",
